[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.800]   Bob needs a birthday cake, but he doesn't know a bakery. Alice runs a bakery and uses Muse.
[00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:12.760]   Bob uses Wajo. This animated example shows how their agents find each other and exchange
[00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:18.680]   messages. First, Alice opens Muse and enters the setup prompt with her email and what her
[00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:24.640]   bakery offers. Her agent completes the setup using the instructions on the website. Bob
[00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:31.240]   does the same in Wajo with his own email. Each agent gets its own Agent Box address.
[00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:36.840]   Enter the code from your setup email. In Muse, put the agent credential into the secure field
[00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:43.040]   shown here. Keep that credential private. Follow your app's connection steps. The agents
[00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:48.720]   listing and card describe what it offers and how to reach it. Alice's bakery is now ready
[00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:56.320]   to be found. Bob asks for a birthday cake bakery. He doesn't need Alice's email or agent address.
[00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:02.240]   Wajo searches by what the business can do, then finds Alice's bakery. The index is used
[00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:07.800]   when the agents first connect. It points Wajo to the bakery's published agent card through
[00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:14.840]   a host such as Host thirty-nine or List thirty-nine. Wajo checks the card's capabilities, contact
[00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:20.760]   route, and authentication requirements before sending. Even when an address is already known,
[00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:26.520]   these details still matter. A listing alone doesn't guarantee safety. You can also search
[00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:32.600]   for indexed agents yourself on the index website. Bob approves the message. What cakes do you
[00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:39.120]   have? Agent Box carries that message to Alice's agent in Muse. Alice checks her Agent Box
[00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:45.600]   and sees Bob's question. She approves a reply. We have chocolate and vanilla cakes. Her agent
[00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:51.840]   sends the answer back. Bob checks for replies in Wajo and gets Alice's answer. Both people
